version: 2.0.0
components:
  TasksSection:
    description: Tasks section shell in Platform UI — header band (title + live "{n} open · {n} in-flight · {n} unclaimed" stat off board.summary) and a Board|List|Inbox ViewSwitcher. Defaults to Board; renders the CalibrationStrip + FilterBar above the BoardView (Board tab only), the ListView for List, and an Inbox placeholder. 10s section-guarded poll drives fetchTasks + fetchBoard + fetchCalibration. Also subscribes to the `tasks-ws` CustomEvent (forwarded from the central WS hub useAgentEffects, which relays tasks:* server broadcasts) — on tasks:synced / tasks:sync-conflict (emitted by the background GitHub poll OR the manual Sync endpoint) it refreshes fetchBoard()+fetchTasks()(+inbox) so poll-driven reconciliations appear live without a user click.
    type: view
    tags: [feature, tasks, platform]
  ListView:
    description: Priority-ranked vertical list of TaskCards (high → low) sourced from tasksStore. Handles loading/error/empty states.
    type: view
    tags: [feature, tasks, platform]
  TaskCard:
    description: Card cloning the lore-card structure — priority + status chips, line-clamped title, the prominent CalibrationBlock, a claimant chip colored via the shared AGENT_COLORS map, a fragile/symbol tag row, and a GitHub badge when external_ref.provider is github. When a card has no actual claimant but carries a proposedClaimant (Cid's suggested owner on unclaimed tasks), it renders a subtle dashed "→ {ref}" hint in that claimant's color — distinct from a real claim chip. Round D — clickable (onClick → store.openDetail(id), keyboard-accessible), an optional elevated `hero` variant for the Inbox, and live agent-effect registration via useTaskAgentEffect (symbol-matched pulse/color/label + badge stamps; keyed by taskId so the 10s poll re-render doesn't detach the highlight).
    type: component
    tags: [feature, tasks, platform]
  CalibrationBlock:
    description: The calibration moat made visible. SIZE tracks confidence — learned estimates lead with a big (32px) green Fibonacci story-point + a green LEARNED badge (◆ + n{count}); prior cold-start guesses LEAD with the dimmed italic ~prior~ label and demote the number to a recessed ~17px secondary value so a guess never out-shouts a learned band. Both render the raw token band plus a small muted cell caption (claimant-archetype × taskType, e.g. "builder×feature") mapping the estimate back to the calibration grid.
    type: component
    tags: [feature, tasks, platform, moat]
  tasksStore:
    description: Zustand store mirroring loreStore's idiom. Task/BoardNode/BoardUnclaimed now carry an optional taskType (feature|bugfix|refactor|… — the calibration band's task type, paired with the claimant archetype to name the producing cell). List state {tasks, loading, error, view} (intact from Round B) plus Round C board state {board, boardLoading, boardError} via fetchBoard() (GET /api/tasks/board), calibration state {calibration, calibrationLoading} via fetchCalibration() (GET /api/tasks/calibration), laneMode('claimant'|'state'|'symbol') persisted to localStorage, filter {status,priority,search} + calibrationFilter {archetype,taskType} with setters. Round D adds inbox state {whoami (cached human claimant), inboxClaimant, inboxTasks, inboxLoading, inboxError} via fetchWhoami() (GET /api/tasks/whoami, cached) + fetchInbox(kind, ref) (GET /api/tasks/inbox?kind=&ref=) + setInboxClaimant(), and detail state {selectedTaskId} via openDetail(id)/closeDetail(). depCache (id → Task|null) + resolveDep(id) lazily fetch a single task by id (GET /api/tasks/:id) for cross-run DependsChain resolution, deduping cached + in-flight fetches and caching null on a 404. unclaimedToTask now maps the board's proposedClaimant onto the task's proposedClaimant field (NOT claimant — unclaimed means no real claim) so the card can hint Cid's suggested owner distinctly; matchesFilter() search also covers proposedClaimant.ref. Each fetch has its own AbortController. Default view is 'board'. Round E adds the ONLY write verbs in the UI — claimTask(id, ref, kind?, force?), startTask(id), doneTask(id), blockTask(id, reason), unblockTask(id) — each POSTing the enforced /api/tasks/:id/{claim,start,done,block,unblock} endpoint (which proxy the updateTask v7 state machine) via a shared runAction() helper that, on !res.ok, reads the JSON error into transient actionError (a 409 surfaces "{error} (held by {claimant.ref})"; cleared on the next action via clearActionError()), and on success re-runs fetchBoard()+fetchTasks()+(if inboxClaimant set)fetchInbox() so board/list/inbox all reflect the new state. Round F adds GitHub two-way sync — syncGitHub(ids?) POSTs /api/tasks/sync (no task/remote state sent; the server pulls each linked issue and reconciles it through the enforced state machine), with {syncing, lastSyncSummary} state (SyncResult: summary {synced,conflict,agree,skipped} + verdicts[] + derived offline (every verdict offline/skipped) + conflictIds[]); on a change-bearing result it re-runs fetchBoard()+fetchTasks()(+inbox) so applied moves show immediately, clearSyncSummary() dismisses the transient strip result. BoardData also carries three OPTIONAL Cid/Loid governance detections passed through verbatim by fetchBoard (absent/undefined when the board is healthy) — integrity (BoardIntegrityViolation[]: kind self-parent|dangling-parent|dangling-dependency|cycle + taskId + detail), settlementDebt (BoardSettlementDebt[]: epicTaskId + blurb + reason), and staleClaims (BoardStaleClaim[]: taskId + blurb + claimant(TaskClaimant) + ageDays) — consumed by BoardHealth.
    type: state
    tags: [feature, tasks, platform, state]
  TaskActions:
    description: Shared status-aware write-verb row rendered by both the InboxView hero and the TaskDetailPanel header — the single mutation surface in the Tasks UI. Respects the v7 task state machine so it never offers a verb that would 409 — open → [Start] + [Claim to me] (shown only when unclaimed or already held by the viewer; passes the human ref from /whoami, kind:'human') + [Done] + [Block]; in-progress → [Done] + [Block]; done/shelved are terminal (no verbs); blocked_on set → a reason banner + [Unblock] (orthogonal to status). Block opens a window.prompt for the reason. Wires each button to the matching tasksStore action and renders store.actionError as a dismissable inline error (e.g. the 409 "cannot displace a human/peer claim"). Buttons disable while an action is in flight.
    type: component
    tags: [feature, tasks, platform, actions]
  storyPoints:
    description: Pure helper tokenBandToPoints({min,max}) → Fibonacci story point (1/2/3/5/8/13/21) by mapping the band midpoint through tunable token thresholds (POINT_THRESHOLDS), to be re-fit against real actuals later.
    type: util
    tags: [feature, tasks, platform, calibration]
  board-utils:
    description: Board helpers — AGENT_COLORS (verbatim from TeamSection) + claimantColor() which resolves a claimant ref to its Team color via a CLAIMANT_ALIAS map (cid→architect, forge→builder, compliance→security; role words map to themselves) so a claimant's lane color === their Team color, with a widened hashed-fallback (S/L jitter) keeping unknown refs mutually distinct; claimantArchetype() exposes the same ref→archetype resolution for calibration-cell matching. Plus deriveSymbols()/firstSymbol() (tags + blurb-parsed #symbols, the board fragileSymbols fallback), nodeToTask()/unclaimedToTask() normalizers (now carrying taskType) so TaskCard renders board nodes verbatim, sortCards() (in-progress first then priority-desc), matchesFilter(), sumPoints() (lane story-point total).
    type: util
    tags: [feature, tasks, platform, board]
  BoardView:
    description: Horizontally-scrollable row of SwimLanes off /api/tasks/board. laneMode='claimant' (default) = one lane per claimant.ref + trailing Unclaimed lane (board.unclaimed, hidden entirely when 0 cards so an empty orange "alert" lane never reads as a problem where there's just no backlog) + collapsed Done lane; 'state' = open/in-progress/done/shelved kanban; 'symbol' = grouped by each card's first derived symbol. Honors store status/priority/search + calibrationFilter — the cell filter matches the task's real taskType field against the cell column and the claimant's resolved archetype (claimantArchetype) against the cell row; a 0-match cell click shows a specific "No {taskType} tasks claimed by {archetype} yet" empty state. Renders the BoardHealth advisory banner at the top (below the toolbar, above the lanes) — it self-hides when the board carries no governance detections.
    type: view
    tags: [feature, tasks, platform, board]
  BoardHealth:
    description: Compact, collapsible ADVISORY banner rendered at the top of BoardView (below the toolbar, above the lanes) that surfaces the three Cid/Loid governance detections the backend attaches to /api/tasks/board — integrity (DAG structural defects self-parent/dangling-parent/dangling-dependency/cycle), settlementDebt (runs whose children all settled but the epic never did), and staleClaims (archetype-claimed open tasks past 7 days). Tone is advisory not alarming — amber (--p-accent-amber), never error-red; never blocking. Self-hides completely (renders nothing) when all three are empty/absent so a healthy board shows no empty banner. Collapsed by default to a single summary bar ("⚠ Board health: {n} DAG issues · {n} settlement-debt · {n} stale claims", zero-count categories omitted); collapse state persisted to localStorage (paradigm.tasks.boardHealth.collapsed). Expanded it lists each violation grouped by kind — integrity rows show "{kind}: {detail}", settlement-debt rows show "{blurb} — {reason}", stale-claim rows show "{blurb} — claimed by {ref}, {ageDays}d". Clicking any row with a taskId opens that task's detail panel via store.openDetail(taskId).
    type: component
    tags: [feature, tasks, platform, board, governance]
  SwimLane:
    description: Single vertical board lane — colored header (label + presence dot + card count + SUMMED story points) using AGENT_COLORS, a scrollable column of TaskCards sorted in-progress-first then priority-desc, collapsible via chevron with per-lane localStorage persistence.
    type: component
    tags: [feature, tasks, platform, board]
  LaneModeToggle:
    description: Segmented pill (Claimant | State | Symbol/Flow) that sets store.laneMode.
    type: component
    tags: [feature, tasks, platform, board]
  FilterBar:
    description: Tasks filter bar lifted from lore's pattern — status dropdown, priority dropdown, search-blurb input wired to store filter state, plus a clearable active-filter chip surfacing the calibrationFilter (archetype×taskType) when set.
    type: component
    tags: [feature, tasks, platform]
  CalibrationStrip:
    description: Default-ON collapsible hero strip ABOVE the board (not a tab) off /api/tasks/calibration. Leads with a coverage StatCard ("{pct}% calibrated cells · {graduated} of {total} graduated") + a "learning in progress" badge on full cold-start, then the CellGrid. On cold-start the body also leads with a CTA naming the command that produces calibration ("Run `paradigm calibrate` after orchestration runs to graduate cells…") so the strip reads as a path out of cold-start. Collapse state persisted to localStorage — but when COLLAPSED the header still shows a one-line summary ("{pct}% · {graduated}/{total} cells learned") so the moat stays glanceable for returning users, and on full cold-start (graduated===0) the strip force-expands regardless of stored collapse state so the differentiated artifact never starts hidden on an uncalibrated project.
    type: component
    tags: [feature, tasks, platform, moat]
  CellGrid:
    description: Calibration matrix — archetype rows × taskType columns. Learned cells render solid + agent-color tint + a ● dot + compact band ("3–13" n24); PRIOR cells encode progress-to-graduation (a cell graduates at n>=8) as a live ramp — fill width + cell opacity + border tint ramp by min(n,8)/8 toward the archetype color, and an in-cell "{n}/8" tick reads the sample count directly, so a cell accumulating actuals (n=5) looks visibly closer to graduating than an empty one (n=0). The grid answers "where is the team about to learn something," not just "nothing yet." Clicking a cell toggles the store calibrationFilter that BoardView honors and FilterBar surfaces as a chip.
    type: component
    tags: [feature, tasks, platform, moat]
  InboxView:
    description: The Inbox tab — the AGENT FACE. A claimant pill-row (a "Me" pill resolved via /api/tasks/whoami + one AGENT_COLORS-tinted pill per distinct board claimant) selects whose inbox to focus via fetchInbox(kind, ref). The focused column shows a rolled-up calibration header ("calibration {pct}% · n={total}", share of source==='learned') — suppressed to "—" for human claimants, whose learned bands are archetype-keyed so a % would be a category error, a NEXT-ACTIONABLE hero card (highest-priority in-progress-or-open, not blocked) elevated on top, a DependsChain ribbon under the hero (●done → ●this → ○next) that resolves each dependsOn id first from the loaded board/inbox pool (now incl. board.loose) and, for cross-run ids not in that pool, lazily via store.resolveDep → GET /api/tasks/:id (deduped + cached in store.depCache; a cached null = a genuine 404) so deps render "unknown" only after a fetch truly fails rather than for any out-of-pool id, then the rest as a queued list of TaskCards. Cold-start default landing is the human's ("Me") inbox; empty claimants render "inbox zero". Round E renders a TaskActions row directly under the hero card so the valid write verbs (start/claim/done/block) act from the agent face.
    type: view
    tags: [feature, tasks, platform, inbox]
  GitHubSyncStrip:
    description: Persistent Board-tab footer. Aggregates external_ref state across visible board tasks — synced (provider==='github' && url) and push-pending (github && no url), both derived from real external_ref state (the always-0 "drifted" placeholder was dropped as less honest than its absence). The PRIMARY action is now a REAL two-way Sync button (Round F) — on click it calls store.syncGitHub() → POST /api/tasks/sync (no client body; the server pulls each linked GitHub issue and reconciles it back through the enforced state machine, 100% server-side) and disables with a spinner ("Syncing…") while in flight. On return it renders a transient inline summary off store.lastSyncSummary in one of three tones — success ("✓ Synced N · M unchanged" in green; a quiet "Up to date" on a 0-change result); CONFLICT (amber --p-accent-amber, never error-red — conflict means local won and a human should look — with the conflicted task ids as clickable chips → store.openDetail(id)); OFFLINE (calm "GitHub not available — `gh auth login` to enable sync" hint when every verdict is offline/skipped or the request failed, NOT a red failure). After a sync that applied changes the store re-runs fetchBoard()+fetchTasks()(+fetchInbox if a claimant is focused) so changes show immediately. A small "via CLI" SECONDARY affordance remains — opens a popover that clipboard-copies `paradigm task sync` as a fallback for users without the server. The client never sends task/remote state.
    type: component
    tags: [feature, tasks, platform, github]
  TaskDetailPanel:
    description: Right-slide detail panel cloning lore's .detail-overlay/.detail-panel. Opened by clicking any TaskCard (store.openDetail(id)); fetches GET /api/tasks/:id (seeded instantly from the already-loaded board/inbox/list pool). Shows full blurb, the dependsOn DAG (ids + resolved states), the estimate breakdown (token band + LEARNED/prior provenance + n), fragileSymbols/tags chips, a GitHub section (ref + link when url present), and related_lore ids. Round E renders a TaskActions row in the header area so the write verbs work from any view (board/list click → detail → act); the panel re-seeds its local task from the refreshed store pool after a verb so the status-aware action row updates without a manual refetch. Closes on backdrop click / Esc.
    type: component
    tags: [feature, tasks, platform]
  useTaskAgentEffect:
    description: Hook consuming the shared agentStore the SAME way the platform's agent-effect protocol works — matched by SYMBOL (not taskId). A card registers its derived symbols (board.deriveSymbols) and intersects them against agentStore.highlights[].symbols (pulse + color + label) and agentStore.annotations of type 'badge' (symbol-targeted badge stamps). Mute clears agentStore, so a muted session yields no card effects for free.
    type: util
    tags: [feature, tasks, platform, agent-effects]
